      "side": 1,
      "message": "From Bazel\u0027s documentation:\n\"A package is a container of targets, which are defined in the package\u0027s BUILD file. Most targets are one of two principal kinds, files and rules.\"\nExpectedBazelRule defines a rule. Actually, I would like to use this term in other places in the code where it is more precise than a more generic \u0027target\u0027.\nThe CLs that use this struct implement notice and package rules, and are not ready yet. If your concern is that this CL adds something unused, I can either delay committing this CL, or use this struct to streamline some already existing tests.",
